page ReverseProxyPage
  Section id:"reverse-proxy-introduction" py:{ xs:6 md:10 }
    Grid columns:{ xs:1 md:"1fr auto" } gap:5 align:"end"
      Grid columns:1 gap:3
        Text size:"xs" weight:"bold" spacing:"widest" color:"muted"
          "SERVER / REVERSE PROXY"
        Title size:{ xs:"3xl" md:"6xl" } weight:"black"
          "Forward through a trusted route"
        Text size:"lg" color:"muted"
          "return reverse forwards an incoming request to an upstream selected from Dowe Cache. The runtime preserves HTTP behavior while preventing request-controlled upstream URLs."
      Button href:"/docs/server" variant:"ghost" scheme:"muted" size:"sm" iconStart:"server"
        "Server documentation"
  Section id:"reverse-proxy-mental-model" p:{ xs:5 md:7 }
    Grid columns:1 gap:6
      Grid columns:1 gap:2
        Text size:"xs" weight:"bold" spacing:"widest" color:"muted"
          "MENTAL MODEL"
        Title size:"3xl" weight:"black"
          "Resolve first, forward second"
        Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
          "Read the request Host, require its route from Cache, then return a URL field from that exact binding. The compiler rejects body, query, header, or optional cache values as upstream authority."
      Code:
        language:"dowe"
        variant:"soft"
        scheme:"surface"
        copyLabel:"Copy Dowe"
        copiedLabel:"Copied"
        content:"""
          import RouteCache from "@/server/config/cache"

          handler forwardRequest
            request host source:"header" name:"Host"
            kv route conn:RouteCache.get key:host required:true
            return reverse:route.upstreams strategy:"roundRobin" state:route.state loadingUrl:route.loadingUrl errorUrl:route.errorUrl
        """
      Grid columns:{ xs:1 md:3 } gap:4
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
            "Trusted binding"
          Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
            "The root binding must come from required Cache.get in the same handler and the return must select one of its fields."
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
            "Validated URL"
          Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
            "The runtime accepts HTTP or HTTPS without embedded credentials or fragments."
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
            "Server only"
          Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
            "Reverse forwarding belongs to the native Dowe server runtime and is not lowered to Cloudflare edge targets."
  Section id:"reverse-proxy-pools" py:{ xs:7 md:10 }
    Grid columns:1 gap:6
      Grid columns:1 gap:2
        Text size:"xs" weight:"bold" spacing:"widest" color:"muted"
          "RUNTIME POOLS"
        Title size:"3xl" weight:"black"
          "Balance only ready nodes"
        Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
          "reverse accepts a Cache-backed array and rotates concurrent requests with roundRobin. Records with enabled:false or a state other than ready never receive traffic."
      Grid columns:{ xs:1 md:2 } gap:4
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"primary" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
            "Loading route"
          Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
            "state loading returns a temporary redirect to loadingUrl while Dowe Runtime verifies and starts the application binary."
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"danger" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
            "Error route"
          Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
            "state error or an empty eligible pool returns a temporary redirect to errorUrl."
  Section id:"reverse-proxy-http" py:{ xs:7 md:10 }
    Grid columns:1 gap:6
      Grid columns:1 gap:2
        Text size:"xs" weight:"bold" spacing:"widest" color:"muted"
          "HTTP CONTRACT"
        Title size:"3xl" weight:"black"
          "Preserve the request and response"
        Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
          "Dowe forwards the method, path, query, body, and safe headers. It removes hop-by-hop headers, sets the upstream Host, and adds the original host as forwarding context."
      Grid columns:{ xs:1 md:2 } gap:4
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
            "Upstream response"
          Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
            "Status, safe headers, and the response body stream flow back to the client without JSON conversion."
        Card variant:"soft" scheme:"surface" p:5 rounded:"md"
          Title size:"lg" weight:"bold"
            "Failure behavior"
          Text size:"sm" color:"muted"
            "A missing route fails before forwarding, an invalid URL is rejected, and an unavailable upstream returns a controlled gateway error."
